    {
      "text": "the same is my brother, and sister, and mother, Matt. 12:50 (Mark 3:35). that a man lay down his life for his friends, John 15:13. affectioned one to another with brotherly love, Rom. 12:10. touching brotherly love ye need not that I write, 1 Thes. 4:9. not as an enemy, but admonish him as a brother, 2 Thes. 3:15. elder women as mothers; the younger as sisters, 1 Tim. 5:2. Not now as a servant, but … a brother beloved, Philem. 1:16. he is not ashamed to call them brethren, Heb. 2:11. Let brotherly love continue, Heb. 13:1. If a brother or sister be naked, James 2:15. Love the brotherhood, 1 Pet. 2:17. compassion one of another, love as brethren, 1 Pet. 3:8. to godliness brotherly kindness, 2 Pet. 1:7. He that loveth his brother abideth in the light, 1 Jn. 2:10. we have … life, because we love the brethren, 1 Jn. 3:14. love God, and hateth his brother, he is a liar, 1 Jn. 4:20.",
